   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the arts and cultural affairs law, in relation to changing New\nYork state history month from November to October",
    "basePrintNo": "S5369",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5369-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 37,
       "fullName": "Shelley Mayer",
       "imgName": "623_shelley_mayer.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1143,
       "sessionMemberId": 1210,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "MAYER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §57.02, Arts & Cul L",
    "lawSection": "Arts and Cultural Affairs Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5369\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the arts and cultural affairs law, in\nrelation to changing New York state history month from November to Octo-\nber\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill changes New York State History Month from November to October\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the Arts and Cultural Affairs Law to establish October\nas New York State History Month Section 2: Sets forth an immediate\neffective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York State History Month was created by the Legislature in 1977 to\ncelebrate the State's unique culture and history. Recently, it has\nbecome clear that November is a problematic month for this celebration.\nMany historical organizations, including most State historic sites, are\nclosed in November and therefore cannot take part in the celebrations.\nBy observing New York State History Month in October, more people will\nhave the opportunity to learn about the State's rich history.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA9560 - 2018.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
